# Symbian E7 harness

Read and follow **AGENTS.md** at the repo root. Drive all device and build work through `./sym`.

## Non-negotiables

1. Start with `./sym doctor` when touching the phone or native SDK.
2. Phone I/O only via `./sym ls|push|pull|deploy|test` — never shell `cp`/`ls` on `/Volumes/NO NAME` (macOS TCC).
3. App args are bare names (`hello`), never `apps/hello`.
4. Prefer WRT (`.wgz`) for fast UI loops; native SIS only when C++/SIS is required.
5. Do **not** rebuild `symbian-sdk:s3` unless `./sym sdk status` shows the image missing or Dockerfile/vendor intentionally changed. Rebuilds are slow and disk-hungry; runtime is Colima **x86_64**.
6. After deploy: tell the user to open **File Mgr → Installs/devdrop** on the unlocked E7.

## Quick commands

```bash
./sym help
./sym doctor
./sym new <name> [--type wrt|native|payload]
./sym deploy <name>
./sym iterate <name>
./sym sdk status
```
